@startuml
title F09 - Main-door history and quiet notice
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #2877B5
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #17324D
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #F4F7FA
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF1BF
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9C6500
autonumber
control "PIR / reed / button hardware" as Sensor
control "N01\nNode sensing" as N01
control "N05\nNode storage" as N05
control "N02\nNode radio" as N02
control "H05\nHub rules adapter" as H05
control "S02\nDeterministic rules core" as S02
control "B07\nRead models/API" as B07
control "B05\nNotification routing" as B05
participant "Web Push provider" as Push
boundary "A02\nApp home" as A02
Sensor -> N01: Reed switch opens or closes
N01 -> N01: Debounce and classify DoorOpen / DoorClosed
N01 -> N05: Persist stable door event
N05 -> N02: Transmit retained event and await durable ACK
N02 -> H05: Deliver committed door evidence through hub ingest/journal
H05 -> S02: Apply event without creating a safety conclusion
H05 -> B07: Project original event time into door history
B07 -> B05: Evaluate explicit opt-in quiet notice policy
B05 -> Push: Send advisory notice once when eligible
A02 -> B07: Fetch door history and evidence freshness
note over A02,Sensor: A door event is advisory household evidence, not proof that a named resident left or returned.
note over Sensor,A02: Outcome - Door activity is recorded once and may create an opt-in quiet advisory without becoming an emergency incident.
@enduml
